---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Gallery from '../../components/Gallery.astro';
import YouTubeEmbed from '../../components/YouTubeEmbed.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Desk"
  description="I wanted a desk that hides most of my computer cables, and one that didn’t take up much floor space."
  image="/images/img_0284.jpg"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Desk</h1>
    </header>
    <article class="project">
      <Gallery
        variant="hero-side"
        images={[
          { src: '/images/img_0284.jpg', alt: 'Finished desk' },
          { src: '/images/desk-ii-front-2.jpg', alt: 'Desk front render' },
          { src: '/images/desk-ii-back.jpg', alt: 'Desk back render' },
        ]}
      />
      <p>
        I wanted a desk that hides most of my computer cables, and one that didn’t take up much floor space. After searching around, I couldn’t find a retail desk that I liked so I designed this in SolidWorks, and then built it. I made a video covering the construction that you can see below.
      </p>
      <YouTubeEmbed id="oKfOzXS5OnY" title="Desk construction" />
      <p>
        The desktop is made out of solid Red Oak, while the rest of the structure is made out of dimensional lumber. The entire table is stained a Dark Walnut color, and then finished with a few coats of oil-based Polyurethane.
      </p>
      <Gallery
        variant="triple"
        images={[
          { src: '/images/leg-bolt-nut-1.jpg', alt: '3D printed leg bolt and nut' },
          { src: '/images/leg-1.jpg', alt: 'Desk leg' },
          { src: '/images/highlighted-leg-connection-e1633828191154.jpg', alt: 'Highlighted leg connection' },
        ]}
      />
      <p>
        The legs are attached to the tabletop with a set of 3D printed nuts and bolts. This allows me to remove the legs in the event that the desk needs to be moved elsewhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        The design of this desk is geared towards an overbuilt look with a wide open tabletop surface, all the while taking up minimal floor space.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
